# #4: Life 1 is always Human; the Character Reset Scroll (Life 2 only) offers the normal races.
# Expect no "ttl:" failure lines. The scroll's own menu list (startingRaces) is checked offline by tests/test_reset_races.py.
ttlbot spawn TtlBotRace
@sleep 4
execute as TtlBotRace run ttl reset TtlBotRace
@sleep 2
ttl racelock TtlBotRace expect tensura:human
# A Life 1 soul that somehow became an elf is set back to Human (the 5 second loop, or this manual run if it came first).
tensura edit race TtlBotRace set tensura:elf
@sleep 1
ttl racelock TtlBotRace enforce
@sleep 1
ttl racelock TtlBotRace expect tensura:human
# The Character Reset Scroll itself is banned in the Mortal Realm: it moves into the soul stash, never stays on the body.
ttl stash TtlBotRace clear
give TtlBotRace tensura:character_reset_scroll 1
ttl stash TtlBotRace sweep
ttl stash TtlBotRace expect banned 0
ttl stash TtlBotRace expect stash 1
ttl stash TtlBotRace clear
ttl reset TtlBotRace
ttlbot remove TtlBotRace
